To clarify:

-my bad, D&D Wizards do have high Int.

-Str modifies both to-hit and damage for melee weapons. The logic
behind this is that dealing lethal damage with a melee weapon is not
based just on whether you can swing your weapon and make it connect
with a monster, it is also based on whether you can hit hard enough to
penetrate armor. Note that your armor does *not* reduce the amount of
damage you deal; it makes you harder to hit.

-Dex modifies both to-hit and damage for missile weapons. The
reasoning for this is obvious. However, there are some weapons, namely
composite bows, that require a certain amount of Strength to wield.

-Weapon Finesse is a feat which causes Dex instead of Str to modify
melee to-hit, but Str still modifies damage. Only certain weapons,
such as rapiers, daggers, and short swords, can be used with Weapon
Finesse.


One of the main reasons I posted this is to see if anyone agrees with
me: Not being able to increase your Int or Cha [i]sucks[/i] until you
start finding cool gear.



